      <ThreatMetaDatum>
        <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
        <Label>Short Description</Label>
        <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
        <Values>
          <Value>Spoofing: an attacker or rogue device pretends to be a legitimate user, controller, field device or server (e.g. rogue master, masquerading, stolen credentials).</Value>
          <Value>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</Value>
          <Value>Repudiation: actions on the control system cannot be traced to a user or device because audit records are missing, shared accounts are used or logs are altered.</Value>
          <Value>Information disclosure: process data, engineering projects, credentials, keys or IP are read by an unauthorised party.</Value>
          <Value>Denial of service: loss of availability, loss of view or loss of control of the process or of a security function.</Value>
          <Value>Elevation of privilege: an attacker gains capabilities beyond those authorised, including crossing zones and conduits or bypassing safety functions.</Value>
          <Value>Abuse is when a legitimate user violates the terms of use for the system without violating a system security policy.</Value>
        </Values>
        <Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id>
        <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
      </ThreatMetaDatum>
