      <Id>PL-T05</Id>
      <ShortTitle>Cyber attack on {target.Name} could drive the process to a hazardous state</ShortTitle>
      <Category>T</Category>
      <Description>If {target.Name} is manipulated, the process could exceed safe limits (overdosing, overpressure, overflow). The question is whether non-programmable safeguards still prevent the hazard.</Description>
      <PropertiesMetaData>
        <ThreatMetaDatum>
          <Name>UserThreatShortDescription</Name>
          <Label>Short Description</Label>
          <HideFromUI>true</HideFromUI>
          <Values>
            <Value>Tampering: unauthorised modification of logic, firmware, setpoints, process values, configuration or messages in transit.</Value>
          </Values>
          <Id>8b1091e7-d25d-5920-b4cb-744fda3aa003</Id>
          <AttributeType>1</AttributeType>
        </ThreatMetaDatum>
